flmusic -- the FreeLFS music player ("Music")
=============================================

    flmusic [--tab albums|artists|songs] [--search TEXT] [FOLDER | FILE...]
    flmusic --ctl play|pause|play-pause|stop|next|previous|status

The library is ~/music (else ~/Music; FLMUSIC_DIR or a FOLDER argument replaces it),
read by tags: Albums (grouped by album artist and album, tracks by disc and number),
Artists, and Songs. FILE arguments are queued and played at once. The search box filters
all three views (title, artist, album).

Playing: double click or Enter on a song plays it with the rest of the list as the queue;
"Play" plays the whole list; "Add to queue" appends it (key A adds the selected song). The
queue panel on the right shows "Up next"; click an entry to jump to it. Shuffle, repeat
(off, one, all), a seek bar and a volume slider are in the bottom bar.

Keys: Space play/pause, Left/Right seek 5 s (Alt+Left/Right previous/next), N and P next and
previous, M mute, S shuffle, R repeat, A add to queue, Q show/hide the queue, 1 2 3 the
three views, Ctrl+F or / search, Ctrl+Q quit. "Previous" restarts a track that is more
than 3 s in.

MPRIS: the player owns org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.flmusic on the session bus with
MediaPlayer2 and MediaPlayer2.Player (Play, Pause, PlayPause, Stop, Next, Previous, Seek,
SetPosition, OpenUri; PlaybackStatus, Metadata, Position, Volume, Shuffle, LoopStatus,
CanGoNext ..., PropertiesChanged and Seeked signals). Any panel or key daemon that speaks
MPRIS works. For the compositor's media keys there is `flmusic --ctl play-pause` (also
play, pause, stop, next, previous, status): it calls the first MPRIS player on the bus, so
XF86AudioPlay/Next/Prev can simply run it. A second flmusic window has no MPRIS (the bus
name is taken).

Formats: whatever GStreamer has (playbin): MP3, FLAC, AAC/M4A, WAV, Ogg Vorbis, Opus
(gst-plugins-base with ogg, vorbis, opus; gst-plugins-good; gst-libav). Output goes to
pipewiresink if the plugin exists, else autoaudiosink; FLMUSIC_SINK=fakesink plays into
nothing (tests).

Tags come from GstDiscoverer, one file per timer tick (the window stays usable), and are
cached in ~/.cache/flmusic/library.tsv with the file's size and mtime, so a restart shows
the library at once and reads only new or changed files. Missing tags fall back to the file
name (title), the folder (album) and "Unknown artist". Album tiles are flat colours with the
album's first letter; embedded cover art is not read yet.

Memory: about 60 MB RSS while scanning and playing (GStreamer and its decoders are most of
it; the interface itself is a few MB).

Test: make check needs dbus-daemon, python3 and the GStreamer plugins: it synthesises a
library (tests/mkaudio.py, tests/tagenc.c), starts a private session bus and drives flmusic
through MPRIS (play, pause, next, previous, position advancing, stop) with a fakesink.
